# Glamsfyt frontend

Follow existing patterns. Do not invent new architecture. These rules are for the Next.js app only. The Express employee service under `src/` follows the backend rules.

**Stack:** Next.js 15 App Router, React 19, TypeScript strict, Tailwind 3.4, NextUI, react-hook-form.

**Scope:** Next.js UI only. Next.js Route Handlers may use Zod. Do not apply this file inside `src/`.

**Server owns:** Zod request and response validation, data fetching in async Server Components and Route Handlers, auth, rate limits.

**Client does not own:** SWR or React Query for page data. Prefer a server fetch. Light client checks are form UX only.

## Structure

```
app/
  layout.tsx, page.tsx, globals.css, constants.ts
  components/          # shared UI
  about|contact-us|solutions|.../page.tsx
  email/route.ts       # API, out of scope
```

- Pages are Server Components. Add `"use client"` only for state, effects, browser APIs, or event handlers.
- Shared data and fonts live in `app/constants.ts`.
- Path alias `@/*` is the project root.
- No new abstraction unless it is reused in two or more places.
- No drive-by refactors outside the task.

## Do not

| Don't | Do instead |
|---|---|
| New `FadeInSection` or Framer wrappers | Plain `<section>` or `<div>` plus Tailwind |
| `<img>` | `next/image` |
| `any` | A real type |
| `style={{}}` for static CSS | Tailwind |
| New CSS modules or CSS files | Tailwind plus existing `globals.css` utilities |
| `router.push` for simple navigation | `<Link>` |
| `"use client"` on a whole page by default | Client only where a browser API is required |
| SWR or `useEffect` fetch for page data | Async Server Component |
| Trust client-only form validation | Zod on the server |
| Blanket `useMemo`, `useCallback`, or `memo` | Only when there is a clear need |
| Index as `key` on a dynamic list | A stable id |
| `console.log` of user data or PII | Remove it, or guard it to development |
| Treat Zod, SWR, or auth as required client deps | Keep the client thin |

## Copy from

- `app/layout.tsx` — shell, fonts, header, footer
- `app/page.tsx` and `app/about/page.tsx` — composition and heading markup
- `app/components/header.tsx` — client nav and drawer
- `app/components/enquiry-form.tsx` — forms
- `app/constants.ts` — fonts and shared data
- `app/globals.css` — `.light-container` and other shared classes

## Before shipping UI

- Plain Tailwind sections. No new `FadeInSection`.
- Mobile-first (`base` then `md:`). Mobile markup first in the DOM when both exist.
- Short Tailwind utilities (`text-lg`, `px-4`). No long class strings unless the design needs an exact value.
- Server Component unless a client API is required.
- Images have `alt` and `width`/`height` or `fill`.
- Forms use react-hook-form for UX. The server validates the payload.
